{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 42, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "**A Whirlwind Adventure in Japan**\n\nJapan is a land where tradition meets futuristic innovation, and my recent trip was a perfect blend of both. The journey began in **Tokyo**, a city that never sleeps. Neon lights flickered in **Shibuya**, where scramble crossings and bustling crowds set the pace. I lost myself in **Akihabara’s** electric alleyways, surrounded by anime, gaming, and cyber cafés. A quiet escape came at **Senso-ji Temple** in Asakusa—its towering gates and incense-strewn streets felt like stepping into another era.\n\nNext, I took the shinkansen to **Kyoto**, where bamboo forests whispered in Arashiyama, and geisha glimpses lingered in the **Gion district**. The **Fushimi Inari Shrine**, with its thousands of vermilion torii gates, was magical at dawn. I sipped matcha in a traditional teahouse, savoring the silence between sips.\n\n**Osaka** stole my heart with its playful energy. Dotonbori’s vibrant signs and takoyaki sizzling on grills made every bite an adventure. The **Osaka Castle** stood proudly, its history echoing through the modern streets.\n\nFinally, **Hiroshima** was a humbling stop. The **Peace Memorial Park** reminded me of resilience, while nearby **Miyajima’s** floating torii gate offered a serene farewell.\n\nJapan’s warmth lies in its details—from steaming ramen bowls to the precision of bullet trains. It’s a country that surprises at every turn, leaving you with memories as vast as its landscapes.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.06550939381122589}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -0.27843376994132996}, {"token": " Wh", "logprob": -0.037113383412361145}, {"token": "irl", "logprob": -0.018043426796793938}, {"token": "wind", "logprob": -4.7801782784517854e-05}, {"token": " Adventure", "logprob": -0.8805687427520752}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -0.08243269473314285}, {"token": " Japan", "logprob": -0.